{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1292538-advice-for-the-current-plot-in-my-game","id":1292538,"title":"Advice for the current plot in my game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-27T11:05:22-08:00","id":1292538,"title":"Advice for the current plot in my game","content":"So the situation is this. We're a semi-mixed cabal. 3 Hermetics of different houses, and a Verbena Set in New York. The current situation is that we were given a mission. Many of &quot;our&quot; (Really their the traditions, but hopefully you get the meaning) cults are being actively subourned by Technocratic operatives, and in addition there appears to be more than a few unaligned orphan mages in the area. We're supposed to find and attempt to convert the orphans, and we're supposed to stop the subversion. <br /> <br /> Our group is all Arete 3 and our spheres are House Flambeau (Forces 3, Prime 2, Matter 2), House Fortunae (Entropy 3, Correspondence 2, Mind 1), House Tytalus (Mind 3, Matter 3, Prime 2), Verbena (Life 3, Prime 3, Matter 2).<br /> <br /> We're mostly all inexperienced players and not really the most skilled or experienced at this kind of cold war ideological espionage game yet, so input would help. Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T05:23:23-08:00","id":1292736,"title":"","content":"A lot of this is based on how I would run a plot like this, so take this with a grain of salt:<br /> <br /> If I were running a game for a group of people new to Mage one of my highest priorities would be introducing them to the themes and elements of the game. That includes defining what the Technocracy is, why they are different from other Mages, and really, what other Mages are like. Your party setup would be a real benefit to me in this regard because you are so narrowly focused. So I would set up both challenges to focus on what you don't know about the people involved. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy Plot would be a mystery. They shouldn't be able to subvert mystical organizations so easily, so they are up to something strange. The problem is your characters aren't really set up to understand what they are doing. You might have the spheres, but you need to know things like how are they getting in, how are they setting up (what are their foci) and how can you detect them. <br /> <br /> The first step there would be getting help and advice. A VA or an Etherite could give you valuable insight on what you are looking for. Even more mystically inclined Traditionalists could be helpful if they have long experience with the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> As for the Orphans, the challenge is getting inside their headspace. You can't convince them if you don't know how they think. Each one could present a different challenge, too. Some would be self taught, others would be looking for answers, still others would have bad experiences with the Traditions. This one is harder to specify because there are a lot of options.<br /> <br /> But I would say that some of your possible approaches are surveillance, finding out Traditions members they already have contact with, or just talking with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T15:03:38-08:00","id":1292864,"title":"","content":"Talking? Bah, when has that ever done anything /s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}